{
  "summary": "Enables safe identical code folding (ICF) linker flags in CMakeLists.txt when supported by the linker and compiler. The build system probes for and appends -faddrsig alongside -Wl,--icf=safe or -Wl,--icf=safe_thunks to executable linker flags.",
  "problem": "macOS release binaries contain redundant copies of identical compiled functions, increasing download sizes and disk footprint without functional benefit.",
  "evidence": [
    "Author measurements in the description and commit message show binary size reductions of '~0.5mb' for bitcoind and '1.3mb' for bitcoin-qt on aarch64-apple-darwin."
  ],
  "dependencies": {
    "depends_on": [],
    "enables": []
  },
  "scope_notes": "",
  "changed_since_previous": "Appended the -faddrsig compiler/linker flag to the ICF test strings to ensure address significance tables are emitted so safe ICF does not fold address-taken functions.",
  "card": "This pull request configures safe identical code folding linker flags (-Wl,--icf=safe / -Wl,--icf=safe_thunks with -faddrsig) in CMakeLists.txt. It reduces Darwin release binary sizes, saving roughly 0.5 MB on bitcoind and 1.3 MB on bitcoin-qt according to the author. The change primarily benefits macOS users downloading release binaries.",
